## Development

```sh
uv sync            # install the project and dev dependencies
make check         # lint + tests
make help          # list all targets
```

### Blender

The project is a Blender **extension** (Blender 4.2 or newer): `extension/` holds the
manifest and the add-on, which `make extension` builds into
`dist/{{ package_slug }}-<version>.zip` together with the wheels of this package
and its dependencies, since Blender never downloads anything. Dependencies must be pure
Python, or need one build per platform.

```sh
make install       # build the zip and install it in Blender, enabled
make uninstall     # disable and remove it
make validate      # check the manifest
```

These need `BLENDER` (path of the Blender executable) in a `.env` file (git-ignored) in
the project root, or in `~/.config/blender-ci.env`:

```sh
BLENDER=/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender
```

Without make, install the zip in Blender with Edit > Preferences > Get Extensions >
the arrow menu (top right) > Install from Disk. Add the permissions the extension needs
(network, files) to `extension/blender_manifest.toml`.

The tests run with the [`bpy`](https://pypi.org/project/bpy/) package, Blender as a
Python module, so no Blender install is needed (`make pytest`, a 250 MB download the
first time). `bpy` 5.2 needs Python 3.13, see `.python-version`. A plain `pytest`
without `bpy` skips the tests that need Blender.

## Releasing

1. Add a `v<version>` entry to `CHANGELOG.rst`, update `VERSION` (`make update-version`) and commit on `{{ release_branch }}`.
2. `make release VERSION=<version>` tags, pushes (triggering the GitHub release workflow) and back-merges into `{{ develop_branch }}`.
